## {{.StoreTitle}} and project

{{if eq .Harness "cowork"}}Slug: the project the user names or confirms, matching `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*$`; never the working directory, a sandbox path. None named: ask once, unless the command accepts a blank slug for the whole {{.Store}}. `<root>` below is `/<slug>/`. No shell helper here: never run shell, use `mark_*` tools only. Store: the local {{.Store}}, served by the `{{.MCPServerKey}}` MCP server; a tool not connected or missing (older server): say so, name the server, stop.{{else}}Slug, root and bound {{.Store}}: the session header `Project slug: ... Project root: ... Bound store: ...`. Header absent, or the user means another project (ask for its directory): run

```bash
"$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry project --dir <project-dir>
```

`<project-dir>`: {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}`"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}"`, or the named directory as one POSIX-safe shell word{{else}}the absolute project directory as one POSIX-safe shell word; never wrap the raw path in literal single quotes{{end}}. Output: `slug=`, `store=`, `state=` (`local`, `bound`, `stale`; stale adds `hint=`), `root=`, `project=` (`known`, `new`, `unknown`; unknown adds `reason=`). Stale (header or line): the bound {{.Store}} is unavailable; relay the hint, stop, never fall back to the local {{.Store}}. {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}Exit 127 (a sandbox, e.g. Cowork): Host-only commands stop; else the slug is the one the user names or confirms (`^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*$`, never the working directory; ask once unless a blank slug means the whole {{.Store}}), the store `{{.MCPServerKey}}` (the local {{.Store}}), no more shell. Any other non-zero{{else}}Non-zero{{end}} exit (no directory, unusable directory name), a missing line or an unrecognized `state`: surface it, stop. `<root>` below is the project root: `/` for the {{.Store}}'s root project, else `/<slug>/`. Project unknown (header or line): the root is the default, unconfirmed; name the reason once, continue. Every `mark_*` call goes through the store's server{{if eq .Harness "claude"}} (`mcp__<store>__mark_*`){{else}} (the MCP server named `<store>`){{end}}; a tool not connected or missing (older binary): say so, name the server, point at `/soul-status`, stop.{{end}}